      "Signal 1 — AI-DD + Refractory NSCLC + LncRNA Target + Ribosome Biogenesis / Effect of PSNEAT1 knockout on gene expression and ribosome biogenesis in NCI-H1299 cells [PSNEAT1 ribosome-biogenesis NSCLC bulk-RNA-seq atlas]: GSE333657 (watcher score 9, n=6, Homo sapiens, bulk RNA-seq 'Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing', pdat 2026/09/07 = 2 days ago, raw CSV files, raw_file_availability 'yes', watcher query 'OpenFold weights' [likely query-routing artifact — actual subject is PSNEAT1/ribosome biogenesis], collected_at 2026-09-08T21:02:57Z) is the FRESHEST NOVEL lncRNA-PSNEAT1 / ribosome-biogenesis / NCI-H1299-NSCLC bulk-RNA-seq atlas in the entire 2026-09-09 hits.jsonl with the ONLY FRESH SCORE-9 entry today — the FIRST NON-RECYCLED score-9 since the GSE326553 Oprm1-A118G breakthrough in id:89 (2026-09-04) broke the recycled-score-9 ceiling. It is a direct AI-DD + refractory-lung-cancer + lncRNA-target-nomination + ribosome-biogenesis-stress input for the BB AI-DD + longevity lane, distinct from id:93 GSE286944 Vimentin-compressive-force mechanobiology single-cell by mechanism (lncRNA-knockout + ribosome-biogenesis vs intermediate-filament + mechanical-force), from id:92 GSE345607 CRISPR-immune-inspired-spatiotemporal-switch by modality (lncRNA-bulk-RNA-seq vs CRISPR-mixed-modality), and from id:91 GSE334010 CTHRC1+ fibroblast lung atlas by mechanism (lncRNA-knockout vs fibrogenic-fibroblast-hub). Lung cancer is the leading cause of cancer-related-mortality worldwide (~1.8M deaths/year, ~2.2M new-cases/year), with NSCLC comprising ~85% of cases and KRAS-mutant-NSCLC (~25% of NSCLC) and EGFR-mutant-NSCLC (~15% in Asian-populations) representing the major molecularly-defined subtypes; refractory-NSCLC (treatment-resistant, post-TKI-resistance, post-immunotherapy-resistance, post-chemotherapy-resistance) remains a major clinical-need with 5-year-survival ~25% overall and <10% in stage-IV-disease. NCI-H1299 is a KRAS-mutant (KRAS-G12C) NSCLC cell line widely used as a model of KRAS-driven-lung-cancer. LncRNAs (long-non-coding-RNAs, >200nt-non-protein-coding-transcripts) have emerged as major cancer-drivers and -targets: MALAT1 (metastasis-associated-lung-adenocarcinoma-transcript-1), NEAT1 (nuclear-enriched-abundant-transcript-1), HOTAIR, H19, ANRIL, XIST, and the PSNEAT1 family (a putative paraspeckle-related-NEAT1-paralog) regulate chromatin-architecture, transcription, splicing, mRNA-stability, translation, and ribosome-biogenesis. Ribosome-biogenesis (the synthesis and assembly of ribosomal subunits, involving rRNA-transcription-by-POLR1/2, rRNA-processing, rpL/rpS ribosomal-protein-synthesis, and 60S/40S-subunit-assembly in the nucleolus) is a fundamental cancer-hallmark (Hanahan-Weinberg-hallmark-of-cancer ‘deregulating-cellular-energetics’ and 'sustained-proliferative-signaling') and a major therapeutic-target-class: the ribosome-biogenesis-stress response activates p53 via MDM2-sequestration-by-ribosomal-proteins (rpL5/rpL11/rpL23 → MDM2-binding → p53-stabilization → cell-cycle-arrest + apoptosis), and CX-5461 (a POLR1-inhibitor from Senhwa-Biosciences, in Phase-I/II-clinical-trials for BRCA-deficient-and-hematologic-malignancies), CX-3543 (quarfloxin, a G-quadruplex-stabilizer that disrupts nucleolin-rDNA-interaction), BMH-21 (a POLR1-degrader), and several ribosomal-protein-inhibitors are in clinical-development as ribosome-biogenesis-targeting-anticancer-agents.",
